        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/khedron/{size}/1870_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-01-26T06:07:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Chaosmancer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/48/1977_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chaosmancer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>With the Matriarch, all of her fowls say that after they are played play the top card of her deck. If that card is also a fowl then you rinse and repeat until you do not draw a fowl correct? I'm pretty sure I know the answer but I want to confirm. Also if she has the mask out then the first time she doesn't play a fowl she can play the top card of the villian deck, possibly starting the whole chain reaction again. This makes it completely possible, especially with my bad shuffling skills, for her to get every single fowl card out on the first turn.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Getting every single fowl card seems very unlikely, but you are correct. &nbsp;It is very common to get many fowl cards out every turn.</p>",
